        <name>markOverloadedTemplateInstantiations</name>
        <param>
          <type>SgNode *</type>
          <declname>node</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Mark any template instatiations that are overloaded (we can&apos;t output these since g++ can&apos;t resolve them). </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This function marks IR nodes that can&apos;t be output because of a bug in the GNU g++ compile. Member functions that are overloaded can&apos;t be resolved in the template specialization. e.g. template &lt;typename t&gt;=&quot;&quot;&gt; <linebreak/>
class <ref refid="classX" kindref="compound">X</ref> { <linebreak/>
 <ref refid="classX" kindref="compound">X(T t)</ref>{}; <linebreak/>
 template&lt;typename S&gt; <ref refid="classX" kindref="compound">X(S s)</ref>{} <linebreak/>
}; </para>        </detaileddescription>
